@api @get_echo
Feature: GET Echo Endpoint URL Query Parameter Validation # features/test_get_echo_url_params.feature:2
  As a QA engineer
  I want to validate the GET /get echo endpoint URL contains query parameters
  So that I can ensure the API correctly reflects the request URL
  @api @get_echo
  Feature: GET Echo Endpoint URL Query Parameter Validation  # features/test_get_echo_url_params.feature:2

  @contract @positive
  Scenario: Verify GET response URL contains query parameters    # features/test_get_echo_url_params.feature:14
    Given the API base URL is configured                         # features/steps/test_response_steps.py:16
    When I send a GET request to "/get" with query parameters:   # features/steps/test_response_steps.py:25
      | key | value |
      | foo | bar   |
      | baz | value |
    Then the response status code should be 200                  # features/steps/test_response_steps.py:56
    And the JSON key "url" should contain "postman-echo.com/get" # features/steps/test_get_echo_url_params_steps.py:13
    And the JSON key "url" should contain "foo=bar"              # features/steps/test_get_echo_url_params_steps.py:13
    And the JSON key "url" should contain "baz=value"            # features/steps/test_get_echo_url_params_steps.py:13

@api @get_echo
Feature: GET Echo Endpoint Structure Validation with Multiple Query Parameters # features/test_get_echo_structure.feature:2
  As a QA engineer
  I want to validate the GET /get echo endpoint response structure
  So that I can ensure the response contains required contract keys
  @api @get_echo
  Feature: GET Echo Endpoint Structure Validation with Multiple Query Parameters  # features/test_get_echo_structure.feature:2

  @contract @positive
  Scenario: Verify GET response is a JSON object with required keys  # features/test_get_echo_structure.feature:14
    Given the API base URL is configured                             # features/steps/test_response_steps.py:16
    When I send a GET request to "/get" with query parameters:       # features/steps/test_response_steps.py:25
      | key | value |
      | foo | bar   |
      | baz | value |
    Then the response should be a JSON object                        # features/steps/test_response_steps.py:77
    And the response JSON should contain key "args"                  # features/steps/test_response_steps.py:82
    And the response JSON should contain key "headers"               # features/steps/test_response_steps.py:82
    And the response JSON should contain key "url"                   # features/steps/test_response_steps.py:82

@api @get_echo
Feature: GET Echo Endpoint Date Header Validation # features/test_get_echo_date_header.feature:2
  As a QA engineer
  I want to validate the GET /get echo endpoint returns a valid Date header
  So that I can ensure the API returns properly formatted HTTP date headers
  @api @get_echo
  Feature: GET Echo Endpoint Date Header Validation  # features/test_get_echo_date_header.feature:2

  @contract @headers
  Scenario: Verify GET response includes a valid Date header   # features/test_get_echo_date_header.feature:14
    Given the API base URL is configured                       # features/steps/test_response_steps.py:16
    When I send a GET request to "/get" with query parameters: # features/steps/test_response_steps.py:25
      | key | value |
      | foo | bar   |
      | baz | value |
    Then the response status code should be 200                # features/steps/test_response_steps.py:56
    And the response should have header "Date"                 # features/steps/test_response_steps.py:69
    And the response header "Date" should be a valid date      # features/steps/test_get_echo_date_header_steps.py:13

@api @get_echo
Feature: GET Echo Endpoint Content-Type Exact Match Validation # features/test_get_echo_content_type.feature:2
  As a QA engineer
  I want to validate the GET /get echo endpoint returns the exact Content-Type header
  So that I can ensure the API contract for content type remains stable
  @api @get_echo
  Feature: GET Echo Endpoint Content-Type Exact Match Validation  # features/test_get_echo_content_type.feature:2

  @contract @positive
  Scenario: Verify GET response status and exact Content-Type header             # features/test_get_echo_content_type.feature:14
    Given the API base URL is configured                                         # features/steps/test_response_steps.py:16
    When I send a GET request to "/get" with query parameters:                   # features/steps/test_response_steps.py:25
      | key | value |
      | foo | bar   |
      | baz | value |
    Then the response status code should be 200                                  # features/steps/test_response_steps.py:56
    And the response Content-Type should equal "application/json; charset=utf-8" # features/steps/test_get_echo_content_type_steps.py:11

@api @get_echo
Feature: GET Echo Endpoint Args Type and Value Validation # features/test_get_echo_args_type.feature:2
  As a QA engineer
  I want to validate the GET /get echo endpoint args type and echoed values
  So that I can ensure query parameters are correctly typed and echoed back
  @api @get_echo
  Feature: GET Echo Endpoint Args Type and Value Validation  # features/test_get_echo_args_type.feature:2

  @contract @positive
  Scenario: Verify GET response args is an object with echoed query parameters  # features/test_get_echo_args_type.feature:14
    Given the API base URL is configured                                        # features/steps/test_response_steps.py:16
    When I send a GET request to "/get" with query parameters:                  # features/steps/test_response_steps.py:25
      | key | value |
      | foo | bar   |
      | baz | value |
    Then the response status code should be 200                                 # features/steps/test_response_steps.py:56
    And the JSON key "args" should be of type "object"                          # features/steps/test_post_form_data_steps.py:11
    And the JSON key "args.foo" should equal "bar"                              # features/steps/test_response_steps.py:87
    And the JSON key "args.baz" should equal "value"                            # features/steps/test_response_steps.py:87

